#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc653f0-653a-51c8-9dde-134e1ea1131e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269831} {:answer/id #uuid "63282b85-24f9-5737-88f6-e544d18bead1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270146} {:answer/id #uuid "d283f88f-ed57-5c59-963f-f49777d28ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271122} {:answer/id #uuid "db49a675-ce1e-57fa-a849-aff9de416a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271188} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb23ab9-9422-51b8-8613-a343d4227bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecb23ab9-9422-51b8-8613-a343d4227bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271348} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfceea30-a8b2-5f6c-aa6e-a6e0d02cdbfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f60fdb9d-cf89-59bd-ad65-e9ec096b82df" :question/math-academy-id "q-140049" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ is a triangular matrix\n- $A$ does not have identical rows\n- $A$ does not have proportional columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2=5\\ne 0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ is not a triangular matrix.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\nHence, if $|A|\\ne 0$ then $A$ doesn't have proportional nor identical rows/columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005e27bf-cb54-5586-9f97-7b38aad175ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326938} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd6a87d-fb02-5806-ae65-64162e9cf218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327321} {:answer/id #uuid "8de5c3ae-cce3-5e55-9356-16f0393d6b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328163} {:answer/id #uuid "df2048ab-aecc-5672-ad82-8817a5b81317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328888} {:answer/id #uuid "f32e69b1-2499-5293-92c5-f46f9bacf57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bd6a87d-fb02-5806-ae65-64162e9cf218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327321} :answer-field/id #uuid "49c4b9a1-7b38-5148-a1f8-07d819c935b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fffc6699-6d6e-50bb-8cc3-7d4f0e3f1d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-42460" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has a zero row\n- $A$ has two proportional columns\n- $A$ has two identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero row.\n\n- $A$ has two proportional columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78b84216-c188-5769-a0cf-2f3c4b5d4fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402863} {:answer/id #uuid "47a2ba38-2156-5dd9-922d-70e7a9112796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402864} {:answer/id #uuid "bf232768-62b0-5a99-b6ae-c2f1d1ac4e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402865} {:answer/id #uuid "5c171a58-43ca-5ac8-896f-be2e38df60c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402866} {:answer/id #uuid "75bb085b-9153-5df0-9e32-3ce23b5de8fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78b84216-c188-5769-a0cf-2f3c4b5d4fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402863} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4619bd4-0fd6-5b0e-85d8-4d713cc4997e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44f28c6-ca93-5246-be2b-1a2725d36e07" :question/math-academy-id "q-43057" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -6 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=3\\cdot (-6)\\cdot 2=-36\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=(-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=-12\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d00532a-c12b-50b9-ad0b-b9f1fa474794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415449} {:answer/id #uuid "44173bde-0fab-57de-b1b3-22d94262de8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415452} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9c1118-9a19-54c3-9683-cf1248dd342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415456} {:answer/id #uuid "7e862f84-0fe3-5f4e-8829-b54fb65649ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415457} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80361a1-690f-54bf-a979-055f8bec64f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has two proportional rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}]}
